@startuml
title 05 — Conversation History & Queries

' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Covers the three ways a user can interact with past conversations:
'
'   SCENARIO A — List all conversations
'     Returns a paginated list of conversations with titles.
'
'   SCENARIO B — Read a single conversation's full timeline
'     Returns every message and event for that conversation,
'     in chronological order.
'
'   SCENARIO C — Reopen a paused conversation
'     Some conversations are paused mid-workflow (the chat input
'     is disabled while a Business Agent is working). The user
'     can request to continue — the Orchestrator checks whether
'     confirmation is needed first.
' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

hide footbox
autonumber "<b>[00]"

skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam wrapWidth 260
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8

skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor        #2D6A9F
  ArrowFontColor    #2D6A9F
  ArrowFontSize     11

  LifeLineBorderColor         #2D6A9F
  LifeLineBackgroundColor     #EAF3FB

  ParticipantBorderColor      #2D6A9F
  ParticipantBackgroundColor  #DAEAF7
  ParticipantFontColor        #1A3A52
  ParticipantFontSize         12
  ParticipantFontStyle        bold
  ParticipantPadding          8
  ParticipantBorderThickness  1.5

  ActorBorderColor            #1A3A52
  ActorBackgroundColor        #B8D6EE
  ActorFontColor              #1A3A52
  ActorFontSize               12
  ActorFontStyle              bold

  GroupBorderColor            #5A9ABF
  GroupBackgroundColor        #F0F7FC
  GroupHeaderFontColor        #1A3A52
  GroupHeaderFontSize         12
  GroupBorderThickness        1.2

  NoteBackgroundColor         #FFF8DC
  NoteBorderColor             #C8A800
  NoteFontColor               #4A3800
  NoteFontSize                11
}

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8

' ─── Participants ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
actor       User  as "User / UI"
participant Orch  as "Orchestrator"
database    DB    as "HANA DB"

' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
alt #EAF6EA Scenario A — List all conversations

  User -> Orch : GET /conversations\n(optional: page size, page number)
  activate Orch

  Orch -> DB : get the most recent event for each conversation\n(one row per conversation, ordered newest first)
  DB --> Orch : latest event rows

  Orch -> DB : load the saved conversation titles\nfor those conversation IDs
  DB --> Orch : title map

  note over Orch
    If a conversation has an AI-generated title (from the strategy
    summary in Diagram 02), that is used. Otherwise the Orchestrator
    falls back to the first message text or "Untitled conversation".
  end note

  Orch --> User : paginated list — conversation ID, title, timestamp

  deactivate Orch

else #EAF0FA Scenario B — Read a single conversation's full timeline

  User -> Orch : GET /conversations/{id}/messages
  activate Orch

  Orch -> DB : get all message and event records for this conversation,\nordered from oldest to newest
  DB --> Orch : full ordered timeline

  note over Orch
    The timeline is reconstructed from two sources in HANA DB:
    • A "timeline node" projection — one row per UI payload (e.g. form,
      button group, text bubble), always showing the latest version of
      each item. This handles the case where a form was updated after
      the user submitted it.
    • Raw event records — used as a fallback if the timeline table has
      no rows for this conversation.
  end note

  Orch --> User : ordered message history

  deactivate Orch

end

@enduml
